{title: Hananiah Son of Uzai}
{subtitle: Nehemiah 3:30; 3:1–30; 4:1–6; 6:15–16}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Uzai [Bb]raised up a son called Hana[Eb]niah
He [F]joined the men to build up the [Bb]wall
The gates were set and the bars were [Eb]placed
We [F]worked in the dust as we heard it [Bb]called
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
U[Gm]zai the goldsmith [Dm]worked with [Eb]care
Hana[Gm]niah the per[Dm]fumer stood [Eb]there
They re[Gm]stored the wall to the [F]Broad Wall [Eb]side
Next to Repha[Cm]iah and the peo[F]ple who [Bb]stayed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Sanballat and To[F]biah were furi[Eb]ous
The [Gm]Ammonites and [F]Arabs were fu[Eb]rious
They con[Gm]spired to [F]throw it into [Eb]confusion
But we [Cm]posted a [F]guard day and [Bb]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
The [Gm]laborers said [Dm]our strength is [Eb]failing
[Gm]Too much rubble and we [Dm]cannot re[Eb]build
But we [Gm]prayed to our [F]God and we [Eb]warned
We kept [Cm7]working though our [F]enemies were [Bb]stern
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
The [Gm]wall was finished in [F]fif-ty-two [Eb]days
The [Gm]nations around [Dm7]us were af[Eb]raid
Uza[Gm]i’s son [Dm7/F]helped close up the [Eb]gaps
We [Cm7]finished the [F]work of the city [Bb]walls
{end_of_verse}

